<style>
@page{margin:1in}
body{font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.45;color:#111}
h1{font-size:20pt;margin:0 0 14pt}
h2{font-size:15pt;margin:18pt 0 8pt}
h3{font-size:12.5pt;margin:14pt 0 6pt}
h4,h5,h6{font-size:11pt;margin:12pt 0 5pt}
p{margin:0 0 8pt}
ul,ol{margin:0 0 8pt 24pt}
li{margin:0 0 3pt}
blockquote{margin:8pt 24pt;padding-left:10pt;border-left:2pt solid #bbb;color:#444}
table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:8pt 0}
th,td{border:1px solid #999;padding:5pt;vertical-align:top}
th{background:#eee;font-weight:bold}
code{font-family:Consolas,monospace;font-size:9.5pt}
hr{border:0;border-top:1px solid #aaa;margin:12pt 0}
a{color:#0563c1}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Word Export QA Project</h1>
<p><strong>Context:</strong> Student research project</p>
<h2>1. Find your research interests</h2>
<h2>2. Narrow a topic and test feasibility</h2>
<p><strong>Broad area</strong></p>
<p>Sleep and learning</p>
<h2>3. Explore the research landscape</h2>
<h2>4. Write and refine the research question</h2>
<p><strong>Question family</strong></p>
<p>Relationship / association</p>
<p><strong>Working research question</strong></p>
<p>What is the association between reported weekday sleep duration and biology quiz score?</p>
<h2>5. Build a systematic search strategy</h2>
<h2>6. Evaluate, read, and extract sources</h2>
<h2>7. Synthesize the literature and justify the study</h2>
<h2>8. Write the literature review</h2>
<h2>9. Choose the research design</h2>
<p><strong>Primary design</strong></p>
<p>Correlational / observational</p>
<p><strong>What this design will and will not allow me to claim</strong></p>
<p>Association only</p>
<h2>10. Define hypotheses, variables, controls, and experimental units</h2>
<p><strong>Outcome/dependent variable</strong></p>
<p>Biology quiz score</p>
<p><strong>Experimental or observational unit</strong></p>
<p>One student</p>
<h2>11. Plan sampling, measurement, validity, and ethics</h2>
<h2>12. Write the method and lock the data plan</h2>
<h2>13. Collect, clean, visualize, and describe data</h2>
<h2>14. Choose and justify the data analysis</h2>
<h2>15. Write the Results section</h2>
<h2>16. Write the Discussion and limitations</h2>
<h2>17. Write the conclusion, abstract, title, and keywords</h2>
<h2>18. Citations, references, and final alignment audit</h2>
</body>
</html>